# L §5.16: cdf takes "a distribution value, a random fact read directly, or an affine form of one; anything
# else is refused (LOAD-RANDOM ...)"; L §8.3 "cdf of a non-affine random value".
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input z: dist
input u01: dist
input u4: dist
input cnt: dist
input q25: num
input two: num
input lvl: num
def c: num = cdf(u01 * u01, lvl) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  z = normal(0, 1) to 1e-9
  u01 = uniform(0, 1) to 0.001
  u4 = uniform(0, 4) to 0.001
  cnt = binomial(4, 0.5)
  q25 = 0.25
  two = 2
  lvl = 0.5
=== expect
refused: LOAD-RANDOM ...
